  "_provenance": "Sheet frame proportions measured off the blank 8298 template (pitch 107.1pt, cubicle 404.8pt tall, ANSI B) and scaled x2.5 so the shared symbol library reads at the same relative size it does on 8513. No device elevation on this sheet was measured from any drawing: every one is computed by stacker.py from the symbol library's own block heights plus the gaps declared below. Gaps are a drafting choice -- measuring 8513 showed the same two CTs spaced 0.944 apart on one deck and 0.772 on the other -- so they are chosen for even spacing rather than recovered.",

  "sheet": {
    "pitch": 5.6,
    "_pitch_note": "The 8298 sheet is two-high, so its 3.78 height:width ratio describes a cubicle holding two breakers. 8478 has one breaker and is single-high, and inheriting that ratio drew a box far too narrow for its height. 5.60 against an 11.50 cubicle gives 2.05, which is about the proportion of real metal-clad 38kV gear.",
    "centreline_from_left": 2.5,
    "_centreline_note": "Just left of centre: the PT branch, relay and test switch all live on the right, the CPT branch alone on the left.",
